### Variables for Disable Challenge Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@jwtToken = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@validUserKey = ABC1234
@invalidUserKey = XYZ9999
@validChallengeKey = 8NctRKY
@nonExistentChallengeKey = MISSING
@otherUserChallengeKey = OTHER123
@alreadyDisabledChallengeKey = DISABLED

### AC1: Successful Challenge Disable
# Tests: Valid JWT token, user owns challenge, challenge is currently enabled
# Expected: HTTP 200 OK with entity key response
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{validChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC2.1: Missing JWT Token
# Tests: Authentication failure - no JWT token provided
# Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{validChallengeKey}}/disable
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC2.2: Invalid or Expired JWT Token
# Tests: Authentication failure - invalid JWT token
# Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{validChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer INVALID_TOKEN_HERE
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC3: User Not Found
# Tests: Valid JWT but user doesn't exist in system
# Expected: HTTP 404 Not Found with correlation ID
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{validChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC4: Challenge Not Found
# Tests: Valid user but challenge doesn't exist
# Expected: HTTP 404 Not Found with correlation ID
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{nonExistentChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC5: Unauthorized Access (Not Owner)
# Tests: User doesn't own the challenge being disabled
# Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized with correlation ID
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{otherUserChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC6: Challenge Already Disabled
# Tests: Challenge is already disabled (enabled=false)
# Expected: HTTP 204 No Content
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/{{alreadyDisabledChallengeKey}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC - Invalid Challenge Key Format (Too Short)
# Tests: Challenge key validation - less than 7 characters
# Expected: HTTP 400 Bad Request with validation error
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/SHORT/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC - Invalid Challenge Key Format (Too Long)
# Tests: Challenge key validation - more than 7 characters
# Expected: HTTP 400 Bad Request with validation error
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/TOOLONG123/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC - Re-disable Same Challenge
# Tests: Multiple disable requests on same challenge
# Expected: First request HTTP 200 OK, subsequent requests HTTP 204 No Content
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/TEST_DISABLE_TWICE/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC - Disable Challenge with Public Visibility
# Tests: Disabling a public challenge
# Expected: HTTP 200 OK - challenge disabled and removed from public visibility
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/PUBLIC_CHALLENGE/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0

### AC - Disable Challenge with Private Visibility
# Tests: Disabling a private challenge
# Expected: HTTP 200 OK - challenge disabled
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/cmd/challenge/PRIVATE_CHALLENGE/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
X-API-Version: 1.0
